{
  "dom_id": "step-q335999",
  "name": "Question 7",
  "problem": "Given that the discrete random variable $X$ has the cumulative distribution function $F(x)$ shown in the table below, compute $P(X=4).$\n\n| $x$ | $1$ | $2$ | $3$ | $4$ |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| $F(x)$ | $\\frac{1}{10}$ | $\\frac{7}{10}$ | $\\frac{9}{10}$ | $1$ |\n\n$P(X=4)=$\n{{field-1}}",
  "worked_solution": "The cumulative distribution function of a discrete random variable $X$ is a function $F(x)$ such that\n\n$$\nF(x)=P(X\\le x).\n$$\n\nSo, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}F(4) & =P(X\\le 4) \\\\  & =P(X\\in {1,2,3,4}) \\\\  & =P(X=1)+P(X=2)+P(X=3)+P(X=4) \\\\  & =P(X\\in {1,2,3})+P(X=4) \\\\  & =P(X\\le 3)+P(X=4) \\\\  & =F(3)+P(X=4).\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}P(X=4) & =F(4)-F(3) \\\\  & =1-\\frac{9}{10} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{10}.\\end{aligned}\n$$",
